  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender and Social Inclusion responsive AA for the mitigation and prevention of flood-related risks on women and other vulnerable groups (WEST)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide protection and non-food item assistance to communities on the basis of early flood warnings in Bardiya and Kailali. This UNWomen project deploys gender equality and social inclusion advisors to ensure monsoon flood response and monitoring plans and preparations are gender-sensitive, socially-inclusive and non-discriminatory. Additionally the project distributes comprehensive relief packages to flood-affected households and deploys specialists to monitor the distribution of humanitarian assistance and the delivery of humanitarian services as part of the anticipatory action pilot. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 1,300 people, including 1,100 women, 200 men.</narrative>
  </description>
